---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Woodland Kin" description="The story behind Woodland Kin — mountain rooted apparel from Big Bear Valley, California.">
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-20">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-10">About Woodland Kin</h1>

    <div class="aspect-[21/9] bg-theme-surface rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-12">
      <span class="text-theme-text-muted text-sm"><!-- TODO: Replace placeholder images with real assets -->[Big Bear Valley Panorama]</span>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-theme-text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Woodland Kin started around a campfire in Big Bear Valley. Three friends — Eddie and Natalie from Fawnskin, Jon from Moonridge — wanted apparel that felt like the forest: grounded, unhurried, and built to last. Not another loud streetwear brand. Something quieter. Something that belonged here.
      </p>

      <p>
        Every design represents a different corner of this valley — Fawnskin, Moonridge, Boulder Bay, Big Bear City, Big Bear Lake, and beyond. Each area has its own pride, its own personality, its own story. But at the end of the day, we all share the same mountains, the same storms, and the same stubborn love for this place. That's the whole idea: we are all kin in this woodland.
      </p>

      <p>
        We print on demand because we believe in making what's needed, not flooding the world with excess. Every order is produced individually, which means less waste, more intention, and a product that was made for you. Our blanks are heavyweight, pre-shrunk, and built for the kind of wear that mountain life demands.
      </p>

      <p>
        A portion of every sale goes to San Bernardino National Forest conservation efforts — because this place gave us everything, and we intend to give back. Woodland Kin isn't a lifestyle brand. It's a community. Welcome to the kin.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
